menuconfig C2USB_I2C_STM32
    bool "c2usb STM32 HAL I2C target driver"
    default y
    depends on DT_HAS_C2USB_STM32_I2C_V1_TARGET_ENABLED || DT_HAS_C2USB_STM32_I2C_V2_TARGET_ENABLED
    select DMA
    select GPIO
    select PINCTRL
    select USE_STM32_HAL_I2C if !C2USB_I2C_STM32_V1 && !C2USB_I2C_STM32_HAL_TARGET_ONLY
    select USE_STM32_HAL_DMA
    help
      I2C target (slave) driver for the STM32 I2C v1 and v2 IPs, using the STM32Cube
      HAL I2C driver with DMA transfers. The DMA channels are reserved in the Zephyr
      DMA driver, which routes their interrupts to the HAL DMA driver.

if C2USB_I2C_STM32

config C2USB_I2C_STM32_V1
    bool
    default y if DT_HAS_C2USB_STM32_I2C_V1_TARGET_ENABLED
    help
      The SoC has the I2C v1 IP. The HAL I2C module of these series is disabled
      in hal_stm32 (due to macro name collisions with <zephyr/drivers/i2c.h>),
      so the HAL I2C driver is built as part of c2usb.

config C2USB_I2C_STM32_HAL_TARGET_ONLY
    bool "Build the HAL I2C driver without controller mode code"
    default n
    depends on DT_HAS_C2USB_STM32_I2C_V2_TARGET_ENABLED
    help
      The HAL I2C driver keeps references to its controller (master) mode DMA ISRs
      from the code shared with target mode, so the controller mode code is linked
      even if unused. This option builds a private copy of the HAL I2C driver with
      those references removed, saving about 1 kB of code.
      Has no effect if the HAL I2C driver is enabled by other users
      (USE_STM32_HAL_I2C), as the controller mode DMA APIs aren't functional
      in the private copy.
      Only applies to the I2C v2 IP, the v1 IP HAL doesn't have this issue.

config C2USB_I2C_STM32_INIT_PRIORITY
    int "c2usb STM32 I2C target driver init priority"
    default KERNEL_INIT_PRIORITY_DEVICE
    help
      Must be initialized after the DMA driver (DMA_INIT_PRIORITY).

module = C2USB_I2C_STM32
module-str = c2usb STM32 I2C target
source "subsys/logging/Kconfig.template.log_config"

endif # C2USB_I2C_STM32
